A. Pr\\\u0027astaro.Comment: 52 page","documentType":"research","doi":"10.1016\/j.nonrwa.2012.04.001","downloadUrl":"http:\/\/arxiv.org\/abs\/1106.0862","fieldOfStudy":null,"fullText":"Not available for public API users.","id":761069,"identifiers":[{"identifier":"394715743","type":"CORE_ID"},{"identifier":"1966528493","type":"MAG_ID"},{"identifier":"oai:iris.uniroma1.it:11573\/355053","type":"OAI_ID"},{"identifier":"54462465","type":"CORE_ID"},{"identifier":"info:doi\/10.1016%2fj.nonrwa.2012.04.001","type":"OAI_ID"},{"identifier":"oai:iris.uniroma1.it:11573\/488854","type":"OAI_ID"},{"identifier":"1106.0862","type":"ARXIV_ID"},{"identifier":"2199820","type":"CORE_ID"},{"identifier":"54374891","type":"CORE_ID"},{"identifier":"oai:arxiv.org:1106.0862","type":"OAI_ID"},{"identifier":"10.1016\/j.nonrwa.2012.04.001","type":"DOI"}],"title":"Quantum Exotic PDE\u0027s","language":{"code":"en","name":"English"},"magId":"1966528493","oaiIds":["oai:iris.uniroma1.it:11573\/355053","info:doi\/10.1016%2fj.nonrwa.2012.04.001","oai:arxiv.org:1106.0862","oai:iris.uniroma1.it:11573\/488854"],"publishedDate":"2011-01-01T00:00:00","publisher":"\u0027Elsevier BV\u0027","pubmedId":null,"references":[],"sourceFulltextUrls":["http:\/\/arxiv.org\/abs\/1106.0862"],"updatedDate":"2024-03-04T08:55:45","yearPublished":2011,"journals":[{"title":null,"identifiers":["1468-1218"]}],"links":[{"type":"download","url":"http:\/\/arxiv.org\/abs\/1106.0862"},{"type":"display","url":"https:\/\/core.ac.uk\/works\/761069"}]},{"acceptedDate":"","arxivId":null,"authors":[{"name":"Brown, Harmon Caril"}],"citationCount":0,"contributors":[],"outputs":["https:\/\/api.core.ac.uk\/v3\/outputs\/229066012"],"createdDate":"2019-10-17T20:10:32","dataProviders":[{"id":12679,"name":"","url":"https:\/\/api.core.ac.uk\/v3\/data-providers\/12679","logo":"https:\/\/api.core.ac.uk\/data-providers\/12679\/logo"}],"depositedDate":"","abstract":"Real Cayley-Dickson algebras are a class of 2\u207f-dimensional real algebras containing the real numbers, complex numbers, quaternions, and the octonions (Cayley numbers) as special cases. Each real Cayley-Dickson algebra of dimension greater than eight (a higher dimensional real Cayley-Dickson algebra) is a real normed algebra containing a multiplicative identity and an inverse for each nonzero element. In addition, each element a in the algebra has defined for it a conjugate element \u0101 analogous to the conjugate in the complex numbers. These algebras are not alternative, but are flexible and satisfy the noncommutative Jordan identity. Each element in these algebras can be written A= a\u2081+ea\u2082 where e is a basis element and a\u2081,a\u2082 are elements of the Cayley-Dickson algebra of next lower dimension. Results include the facts that for each real Cayley-Dickson algebra a\u2071a\u02b2 = a\u2071\u207a\u02b2 and (a\u2071b)a\u02b2 = a\u2071(ba\u02b2) for all integers i,j and any a,b in the algebra. The major result concerns zero divisors.... --Abstract, page ii","doi":null,"downloadUrl":"https:\/\/core.ac.uk\/download\/229066012.pdf","fieldOfStudy":null,"fullText":"Not available for public API users.","id":67198489,"identifiers":[{"identifier":"oai:scholarsmine.mst.edu:doctoral_dissertations-3090","type":"OAI_ID"},{"identifier":"229066012","type":"CORE_ID"}],"title":"Structure of zero divisors, and other algebraic structures, in higher dimensional real Cayley-Dickson algebras","language":{"code":"en","name":"English"},"magId":null,"oaiIds":["oai:scholarsmine.mst.edu:doctoral_dissertations-3090"],"publishedDate":"1972-01-01T08:00:00","publisher":"Scholars\\u27 Mine","pubmedId":null,"references":[],"sourceFulltextUrls":["https:\/\/scholarsmine.mst.edu\/cgi\/viewcontent.cgi?article=3090\u0026context=doctoral_dissertations"],"updatedDate":"2022-01-09T23:16:46","yearPublished":1972,"journals":[],"links":[{"type":"download","url":"https:\/\/core.ac.uk\/download\/229066012.pdf"},{"type":"reader","url":"https:\/\/core.ac.uk\/reader\/229066012"